WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:06.380
Let's go to our caller from the FORO for who's
calling today from 4 0 4.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.610
Hey, David, it's Dustin from Atlanta.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.129
Hey, Dustin.

00:00:11.129 --> 00:00:16.920
Just hey, I just wanted your take on this.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:21.290
So the whole never Biden crew.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:27.470
I do get their sentiments, but I don't I can't
for the life of me.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.510
And I know you feel similar to the.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:33.980
Understand the logic behind that.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:40.030
And I was just wondering if you could further
explain your thoughts, because I don't want

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:45.289
to feel like I'm the weird one for not voting
or for voting for Biden if it comes down to

00:00:45.289 --> 00:00:46.289
that.

00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:49.050
You know, so what you want to hear from me,
why I think it makes sense to vote Biden or

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.429
what I think is motivating the never Biden
people.

00:00:52.429 --> 00:00:55.899
Just a little bit of both to share your take
on.

00:00:55.899 --> 00:00:56.899
OK.

00:00:56.899 --> 00:01:00.539
So the never Biden people fall into a few
different categories.

00:01:00.539 --> 00:01:06.260
You've got never Biden people who are of the
mindset that if it's not someone has left

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:10.970
this, Bernie, they might as well let it be
another four years of Trump.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:14.930
So there's folks that are sort of not really
making much of a distinction between Biden

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:18.580
and Trump saying if it's either of them, it's
basically the same thing.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.580
I don't care.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:20.580
I'm opting out, whatever.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.310
So that's that's one group.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:28.000
You've got another group that says, I would
conceivably vote for Biden, but I can't allow

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.790
my vote to be a blank check for the Democratic
Party.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:35.560
So just because Bernie lost doesn't mean I
automatically go to Biden.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:41.310
Biden needs to do do something either needs
to adopt some Bernie policy or reach out to

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:48.070
me in some way or something like that, because
they don't want the DNC to assume their vote

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:50.550
without having to actually work for it.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.730
It is sort of another group.

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:57.280
Then you've also got, you know, kind of more
anarchistic types of the burn it all down

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.000
to build that back up mentality.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.530
I don't think that's a predominant amount.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.250
I also don't think that that's a strategy
that has really served us well in the past.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:07.350
So for me, my approach is the following.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.780
This is not about vote blue, no matter who.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.200
And in fact, if we weren't talking about Biden
or Bernie versus Trump, but we were talking

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.890
about someone terrible, I wouldn't vote for
that person if the person was worse than Trump.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:21.050
I wouldn't vote or I would vote for Trump.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:24.660
We're dealing and we've been dealing for a
while, all with candidates who would be better

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.660
than Trump.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:30.420
So for me, it's not about did Biden earn my
vote or whatever.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:36.051
It's the choices are unless something completely
insane happens because of Corona virus, the

00:02:36.051 --> 00:02:38.730
choices are Biden or Trump.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.440
And Biden is clearly better.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.280
Biden's better on Supreme Court justices.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.480
Biden's better on taxes.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.480
Biden's better on climate.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.480
Biden.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:46.480
Right.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.480
So is Biden the most progressive guy?

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.480
Of course not.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.709
But you're giving me a choice.

00:02:49.709 --> 00:02:54.270
And there's no way that I can morally justified
taking any action that makes it more likely

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.560
Trump will be reelected.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:56.560
That's my view.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.560
OK.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:58.560
Yeah.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.560
Kids, I see.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.130
I mean, a lot of Facebook groups.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:06.220
You know, the Twitter.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:09.880
Stuff about Bernie and the Facebook groups.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:18.510
There's a large there's a large group of people
that feel feel the same way as the Knepper

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:19.510
Biden people.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:24.390
I mean, it's it's really it's gotten extreme
the way I've seen it kind of.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:25.390
Yeah.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.390
Manifest.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:29.959
The only thing I disagree with you, the one
thing I would say is in the same way that

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:32.520
Twitter and Reddit.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:37.060
Overstated how much support Bernie was going
to have in the primary when that support we

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:41.319
saw topped out the Never Biden stuff is also
over-represented.

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:45.270
Now, the thing is you don't need that much
of it to help Trump because a lot of these

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.570
states are going to be very close.

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:51.040
So a little bit of never Biden stuff from
the left in Michigan could give Michigan to

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.040
Trump.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.250
I don't want to pretend that it doesn't matter.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.550
I just think it's important not to believe
that there's way more of that stuff than there

00:03:56.550 --> 00:04:00.000
actually is, but there may well be enough
to give the election to Trump.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.069
OK, well, thank you for taking my question,
David.

00:04:04.069 --> 00:04:05.069
Thank you for calling in.

00:04:05.069 --> 00:04:06.329
I appreciate hearing from you.

